## lifeos-node config (issue #141). Copy to `.env`, fill in, then
## `docker compose up -d --build`. See docs/MANUAL-SETUP.md #141 for the walk-through.

## ---- REQUIRED: keyless AI auth --------------------------------------------
## Mint on ANY machine already logged into Claude (`claude` CLI installed):
##   claude setup-token
## It prints a long-lived subscription OAuth token. Paste it here. This is the
## ONLY credential the node needs - there is deliberately no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

## ---- REQUIRED: pick ONE database mode -------------------------------------
## (a) Turso primary - use this for multi-node / true "Mac off" operation. Both
##     values come from your Turso database (issue #141 calls these
##     TURSO_DATABASE_URL / TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN; the code reads TURSO_URL /
##     TURSO_TOKEN, matching lifeos-api). The node connects pure-remote, so the
##     atomic claim stays server-side and concurrent nodes never double-run.
TURSO_URL=
TURSO_TOKEN=
##
## (b) Mounted file - single node only. Leave TURSO_URL/TURSO_TOKEN empty above,
##     and point this at a directory holding lifeos.db (mounted to /data). SQLite
##     file locking is not safe to share across hosts, so use mode (a) for >1 node.
LIFEOS_DB_DIR=./data

## ---- Node identity ---------------------------------------------------------
## Stamped into every `job.claimed` event so you can tell which node ran a job.
LIFEOS_NODE_ID=lifeos-node-1

## ---- Optional: Telegram announcements --------------------------------------
## Same token as the Worker's BOT_TOKEN. Without it, results are logged locally.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_ADMIN_CHAT_ID=

## ---- Loop tunables (safe to leave at defaults) -----------------------------
LIFEOS_DRAIN_POLL_SECS=3
LIFEOS_DRAIN_STUCK_TTL_SECS=300
LIFEOS_DRAIN_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3

## NOTE: LIFEOS_BUILD_PIPELINE is intentionally NOT here. It is hardcoded to "0"
## (untrusted-node posture) in docker-compose.yml. Flipping it to "1" marks the
## node trusted to run self-extension codegen - only do that by editing the
## compose file directly, for a box you trust as much as the Mac.
